          {
            "id": "p7-q10-short-reason",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Every possible sum is a multiple of 9; 1503 is the closest, and 142 + 375 + 986 achieves it.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let $h$, $t$ and $u$ be the sums of the hundreds, tens and units digits respectively. Each digit from 1 to 9 is used once, so\n$$\\begin{align*}h+t+u&=1+2+3+4+5+6+7+8+9\\\\h+t+u&=45.\\end{align*}$$\nThe total $S$ therefore satisfies\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=100h+10t+u\\\\S&=99h+9t+(h+t+u)\\\\S&=99h+9t+45\\\\S&=9(11h+t+5).\\end{align*}$$\nThus every possible total is a multiple of 9. The multiples immediately below and above 1500 are 1494 and 1503, which are 6 and 3 away respectively. The closer total can be achieved:\n$$142+375+986=1503.$$\nThese three numerals use each digit from 1 to 9 exactly once, so the required value is $1503$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 124
